@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ The same preset applied to matching originals produces the same initial and map
 
 **Editors → Frame addons** lists frame attachments, roof racks and service equipment with the same table, description and source-property view as Addons and Cargo. The main table shows cargo slots, fuel/water capacity, repair points, spare wheels, price, unlock rank, exploration lock, install socket, content and ID, with shared column sorting/filtering. Selecting a row shows all XML properties and source files below. Explicit file parents supply inherited summary values; templates remain visible without expansion, so blanks are unresolved rather than assumed zero. Install sockets do not establish complete truck compatibility.
 
-The **Fuel multiplier** slider uses Truck properties' shared calculations: 0.5×–3× in 0.5 steps. Moving it only selects the factor; **Multiply all fuel** multiplies the current preview of every frame addon with a locally explicit fuel capacity and category, rounds to the nearest 5 litres (ties upward), and clamps to 5–100,000 L. Repeated clicks multiply again; column filters do not restrict the operation. Blank/inherited capacities stay unchanged. Changed fuel cells show the preserved original in parentheses, with amber preview/staged and green applied highlights. **Stage changes** saves an explicit snapshot across restarts; only **Start → Apply pending changes** writes it to the updated overlay. Later previews do not change the staged snapshot. **Revert unstaged edits** restores that snapshot, **Revert staged changes** clears it, and **Reset to original values** previews rounded baseline capacities. Reload discards unstaged previews. Apply validates every fuel target before writing, preserves unrelated XML/templates and original files, and retains staged edits if a capacity changed externally.
+The **Fuel multiplier** slider uses addon-specific bounds: 0.5×–3× in 0.5 steps. Moving it only selects the factor; **Multiply all fuel** multiplies the current preview of every frame addon with a locally explicit fuel capacity and category, rounds to the nearest 5 litres (ties upward), and clamps to 0–10,000 L, skipping zero capacities. Repeated clicks multiply again; column filters do not restrict the operation. Blank/inherited capacities stay unchanged. Changed fuel cells show the preserved original in parentheses, with amber preview/staged and green applied highlights. **Stage changes** saves an explicit snapshot across restarts; only **Start → Apply pending changes** writes it to the updated overlay. Later previews do not change the staged snapshot. **Revert unstaged edits** restores that snapshot, **Revert staged changes** clears it, and **Reset to original values** previews exact baseline capacities. Reload discards unstaged previews. Apply validates every fuel target before writing, preserves unrelated XML/templates and original files, and retains staged edits if a capacity changed externally.
 
 A **slot-based upgrade randomizer** is available in **Randomizer â†’ Upgrades**. Randomize upgrades builds the full component catalog from the workspace, resolves composite tire IDs, uses current obtainable map-truck previews plus direct garage/contract rewards, and saves a draft under `workspace/upgrade-randomization/draft.json`. Region progression must be finalized. Only owned regions are generated; replacement eligibility uses enabled trucks and explicit tire-pack ownership. Each pickup retains its original type, and metal detectors stay fixed. Truck-specific slots prefer unused local-compatible parts; shared slots use all eligible shared parts without a purchase-only restriction, with an extra foreign preference in the first region. Fallbacks broaden the same-type pool before reuse. Stock/default-only and objective-locked replacements are excluded conservatively. There is no locality quota. See [the planner and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
 
@@ -125,3 +125,5 @@ Editors > Addons shows current (original) values for Price, Unlock rank and Expl
 Editors > Addons follows Truck properties for Price, Unlock rank and Exploration unlock: editable cells, current (original) formatting, green applied/amber preview highlights, Reset selected to original, Reset to original values across both views and filters, Stage changes, Revert unstaged edits and Revert staged changes. Reset restores all three supported properties, including removing local attributes absent from the original. Price accepts whole numbers 0-100,000,000, rank 0-30, exploration true/false; blank restores inheritance. Each staged property identifies its source file, definition variant and attribute; legacy exploration-only snapshots remain readable. Other metadata and physical component parameters remain visible as source properties; engines and winches retain their specialized editors. Apply writes the workspace only, with original files preserved.
 
 Truck properties, Addons and Frame addons each have a Show changed only toggle button. It includes preview/staged differences from current files and applied values differing from preserved originals. In Frame addons this includes fuel and tracked price/rank/exploration changes. It combines with header filters and stays enabled across reloads and addon-view switches; turning it off retains other filters. The toggle changes visibility only: Stage and global reset actions still include hidden rows.
+
+Frame addon fuel multiplication skips explicit zero capacities, rounds nonzero results to 5 L, and uses 0-10,000 L bounds. Restoring fuel keeps the exact original integer capacity without rounding it. Truck fuel bounds are unchanged. Truck properties reset also preserves original attribute absence: an introduced UnlockByExploration=false is staged as an attribute removal, so Start no longer retains Not present -> false after reset/apply. XML difference auditing compares parsed properties and ignores whitespace, line-ending and encoding-only differences; real added/removed/changed attributes remain listed.
